{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
As I [G]walked out in the [D]streets of La[G]redo,
As I [G]walked out in La[D]redo one day,
I [G]spied a poor [D]cowboy all [G]wrapped in white [C]linen
All [G]wrapped in white [D]linen as cold as the [G]clay.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
"I [G]see by your outfit [D]that you are a [G]cowboy,"
These [G]words he did say as I [D]boldly stepped by.
"Come [G]sit down be[D]side me and [G]hear my sad [C]story;
I was [G]shot in the breast and I [D]know I must [G]die."
{end_of_verse}
